{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c properties and indexers c properties and indexers","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md","fileName":"C# Properties and Indexers.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Properties and Indexers","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 21:16\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[C Sharp Object-Oriented Type Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Object-Oriented Type Design","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c properties and indexers c properties and indexers","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md","fileName":"C# Properties and Indexers.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Properties and Indexers","heading":"C# Properties and Indexers","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A C# property exposes get and optional set behavior with field-like syntax. Its accessors can calculate a value, validate an assignment, or encapsulate a backing field while keeping callers independent of the implementation.\n\nAn indexer applies similar accessor behavior to bracket syntax, letting an object retrieve or assign values by a key or position. Properties and indexers preserve an interface that is convenient to use without surrendering control over how state is obtained or changed.\n\nA property exposes `get` and `set` accessors around a value and can limit reading or writing independently. An automatically implemented property removes repetitive backing-field code when no custom validation or transformation is needed.","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Object-Oriented Type Design","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"c properties and indexers c properties and indexers","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/C# Properties and Indexers.md","fileName":"C# Properties and Indexers.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"C# Properties and Indexers","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf]]\n\n[[c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["C Sharp Object-Oriented Type Design","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}